>
  <p>The free SEO audit resources are a 50-check PDF plus blank Markdown files for reporting, prioritisation and implementation tracking. They do not include an Excel workbook or automatic SEO score.</p>

  <p>Use the PDF to guide coverage and the editable files to record evidence. The broader <a href="/website-audit-checklist/">web checklist</a> contains 66 checks across disciplines; this page focuses on the SEO audit workflow.</p>

  <h2 id="what-the-template-covers">What the Template Covers</h2>

  <p>The resource set separates checking from decision-making. That keeps a failed check from becoming a high-priority recommendation without evidence.</p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>50-check PDF:</strong> a portable checklist for technical, on-page, content and off-page review.</li>
    <li><strong>Audit report template:</strong> fields for scope, evidence period, limitations, findings and follow-up.</li>
    <li><strong>Prioritisation worksheet:</strong> fields for impact, confidence, effort, dependencies, risk and success checks.</li>
    <li><strong>Implementation tracker:</strong> status definitions plus owners, affected URLs, acceptance criteria and production verification.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="how-to-use-the-template">How to Use the Template</h2>

  <p>Start by defining the domain, subdomains, markets, page sample and evidence period. Run the relevant crawl and platform checks only after the scope is fixed.</p>

  <ol>
    <li><strong>Collect:</strong> export crawl results and relevant Search Console data with dates and filters recorded.</li>
    <li><strong>Verify:</strong> reproduce important findings on representative URLs and distinguish observations from possible causes.</li>
    <li><strong>Prioritise:</strong> assess business impact, evidence confidence, implementation effort and dependencies.</li>
    <li><strong>Assign:</strong> give each accepted task an owner, observable acceptance criteria and a review date.</li>
    <li><strong>Retest:</strong> confirm the released change in production before recording a finding as verified.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="technical-seo-section">Technical SEO Section</h2>

  <p>Technical checks establish whether search engines can discover, crawl, render, canonicalise and index the intended URLs. Record the response, directive or rendered output that supports each finding.</p>

  <p>Compare sitemap and crawl URLs with the intended indexable set. Use Google's <a href="https://support.google.com/webmasters/answer/7440203">Page indexing report</a> and URL Inspection for Google-specific evidence. An exclusion label suggests a line of investigation; it does not by itself prove content quality or crawl-budget failure.</p>

  <h2 id="on-page-seo-section">On-Page SEO Section</h2>

  <p>On-page checks map one page to one clear search task. Review the title, description, H1, section headings, main answer, media alternatives and contextual internal links together.</p>

  <p>A fixed character count or keyword position is a diagnostic clue rather than a pass/fail standard. Google may rewrite title links and snippets, so compare the rendered page with actual search appearance and query data.</p>

  <h2 id="content-quality-section">Content Quality Section</h2>

  <p>Content checks evaluate accuracy, completeness, purpose, evidence and maintenance needs. Google explains that E-E-A-T is a set of assessment concepts rather than a single ranking score in its <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/fundamentals/creating-helpful-content">people-first content guidance</a>.</p>

  <p>Record the page's intended reader task and whether the content completes it. A low word count, old date or low traffic total is not enough to label a page thin, stale or removable.</p>

  <h2 id="off-page-seo-section">Off-Page SEO Section</h2>

  <p>Off-page checks review links and mentions in context. Preserve links that support discovery, referral traffic or authority and investigate suspicious patterns before using Google's disavow tool.</p>

  <p>Record the data provider and export date because backlink indexes differ. Treat third-party authority and toxicity scores as vendor metrics rather than Google measurements.</p>

  <h2 id="scoring-system">Scoring System</h2>

  <p>These downloads do not calculate a universal SEO health score. The prioritisation worksheet uses impact, confidence and effort as documented judgements so reviewers can challenge the evidence behind the order.</p>

  <p>Address confirmed outages, unintended indexing blocks and broken primary actions first. Investigate uncertain causes before recommending broad URL, content or link changes.</p>

  <h2 id="customising-the-template">Customising the Template</h2>

  <p>Copy the Markdown files into a document system or convert their fields into ticket or spreadsheet columns. Keep finding IDs stable and add fields only when they change a decision.</p>

